<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korean H1 energy demand up 3.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>South Korean H1 energy demand up 3.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's energy demand grew 3.6 percent to 84.74 million tonnes of oil equivalent (TOE) in the first half of 1997 from 81.75 million a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Friday.</p>
<p>This compares with an 11.1 percent gain last year.</p>
<p>Energy consumption slowed due to an economic downturn and energy conservation program, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>Breakdown of South Korea's demand for energy resources in the first half, compared with the same period last year. (Figures in brackets are percentage year-on-year growth):  </p>
<p>				   H1 1997		 H1 1996</p>
<p> Total			84,736   (3.6)	81,753  (11.1)</p>
<p>(in thousand TOE)</p>
<p> Petroleum products    369,444   (1.9)     362,522   (7.6)</p>
<p>(in thousand barrels)</p>
<p> LNG			   6,144  (30.7)	 4,702  (33.1)</p>
<p>(in thousand tonnes)</p>
<p> Hard coal		   1,725 (-19.4)	 2,139 (-17.8)</p>
<p>(in thousand tonnes)</p>
<p> Bituminous coal	  22,691   (4.2)	21,768  (18.7)</p>
<p>(in thousand tonnes)</p>
<p> Nuclear power	    34,539  (-2.9)	35,561  (11.8)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Hydroelectric power     2,378  (-3.6)	 2,467  (18.9)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Other			   645  (15.5)	   558   (9.9)</p>
<p>(in thousand TOE)</p>
<p>(Source: Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy).</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
